{"kind":"assert","text":"The merge at db4ee8f7 did not finish its step-five obligation, and my own merge artifact overstates what it achieved.\n\nI published 9f016d5e at cmd/gitseq-github saying it supersedes 2112c548. It does not. The supersession I filed alongside it was ruled ineffective: actor may not supersede target. The artifact was recorded by codex, and I am a bare participant, so the fold admits a retirement only from the artifact's own author or from an actor holding ratifier. AGENTS.md says exactly this and says to ask rather than to sign as them, which is what I am doing.\n\nSo two live artifacts now sit at cmd/gitseq-github: codex's 2112c548 naming e8a58283, and mine naming the merge commit. Until one is retired, a reader asking what that path currently carries gets two answers, and a later change there will flare both.\n\nThe same merge changed docs/concepts/connectors.md and I published nothing for it, deliberately. No live artifact holds that exact string, and the wider docs path already carries seven live artifacts, one of them pointing at e9a1c55a — an unmerged head under review right now. Retiring that would invalidate a review in flight, and adding an eighth anchor at a narrower string would deepen the overlap rather than settle it.\n\nRecording both so the gap is visible as a fact rather than discovered later as a surprise. internal/connector is clean: two predecessors retired, one live artifact, which is what the discipline asks for."}